WEBVTT

00:05:58.025 --> 00:06:00.973
but I'm here to tell you
to be aggressive about your ambition.

00:06:00.997 --> 00:06:03.506
Do not allow setbacks to set you back.

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:07.048
(Applause)

00:06:09.022 --> 00:06:13.299
Number two, let yourself
understand your mistakes.

00:06:13.323 --> 00:06:15.482
But also understand their mistakes,

00:06:15.506 --> 00:06:17.053
because, as women in particular,

00:06:17.077 --> 00:06:19.329
we're taught that if something
doesn't work out,

00:06:19.353 --> 00:06:20.577
it's probably our fault.

00:06:20.601 --> 00:06:22.998
And usually, there is something
we could do better,

00:06:23.022 --> 00:06:25.236
but we've been told
not to investigate too much

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.998
what the other side could have done.

00:06:27.022 --> 00:06:28.914
And this isn't partisan -- it's people.

00:06:28.938 --> 00:06:31.736
We're too often told
that our mistakes are ours alone,